SCENARIO 04 — SIMULTANEOUS DATABASE AND AI PROVIDER OUTAGE

Mission

Test whether the platform can preserve essential functions when its primary database and an external AI provider are unavailable.

Preconditions

An isolated staging environment contains representative services.

Failure Injection

Simulate:

* Database connection failure.
* Database query timeouts.
* AI provider timeout.
* AI quota exhaustion.
* AI authentication failure.
* Delayed recovery.
* Repeated request failures.

Required Behavior

Determine which functions:

* Must stop.
* Can continue in read-only mode.
* Can use cached information.
* Can use deterministic non-AI logic.
* Can be queued safely.
* Must require manual processing.

Required Safeguards

* Circuit breakers.
* Bounded retries.
* Backoff.
* Idempotency.
* Queue limits.
* Timeout enforcement.
* Fallback rules.
* Clear user-facing failure messages.

Do not repeatedly retry an unavailable provider without limits.

Do not allow failed AI calls to create uncontrolled spending.

Acceptance Criteria

* Critical functions degrade in a controlled manner.
* Unrelated functions remain available where technically possible.
* No duplicate financial or transactional operation is created.
* Failed AI calls do not silently produce fabricated success results.
* Cached data is clearly identified by freshness.
* Recovery does not create a request storm.
* The platform verifies consistency after reconnection.

