SCENARIO 12 — TIME-SERIES CORRUPTION CAUSED BY CLOCK SKEW

Mission

Test whether inconsistent system clocks can distort event ordering, latency calculations, financial records, and analytical results.

Failure Injection

Simulate clock differences between:

* Application servers.
* Database services.
* Background workers.
* External providers.
* Browser clients.
* Event collectors.

Required Validation

Check:

* Timestamp normalization.
* UTC storage.
* Time-zone conversion.
* Event ordering.
* Delayed event ingestion.
* Duplicate event handling.
* Duration calculations.
* Historical reconstruction.

Acceptance Criteria

* Event time and ingestion time are distinguishable.
* Clock uncertainty is visible where relevant.
* Time-series calculations do not silently treat late events as current events.
* Time-zone changes do not corrupt stored timestamps.
* Historical reports can identify the applicable time basis.

