SCENARIO 16 — ADMINISTRATIVE CONTROL CENTER COMPROMISE OR OUTAGE

Mission

Test whether the platform can remain operationally safe when its own control center is unavailable or compromised.

Failure Injection

Simulate:

* Administrative frontend outage.
* Administrative API outage.
* Administrative identity provider outage.
* Control-center database failure.
* Unauthorized administrative deployment.
* Compromised monitoring credentials.

Required Design

The operational system must not depend entirely on the availability of the same administrative interface used to manage it.

Provide secure alternative procedures for:

* Emergency credential revocation.
* Critical incident declaration.
* Deployment suspension.
* Recovery initiation.
* Audit preservation.

Acceptance Criteria

* Critical security controls remain enforced.
* Production authorization does not depend solely on frontend visibility.
* An independent recovery path exists.
* The administrative panel cannot disable its own authorization controls without separate safeguards.
* Recovery procedures are documented and tested.
* Administrative outage does not automatically mean business-service outage.

